{
  "owner": "consus-launcher/policy/model-choice-cases.json",
  "spec": "consus-launcher docs/device-policy-models-and-custom-connectors.md, \"Model order\"; consus-key-portal specs/launcher-settings-page.md",
  "about": "Shared cases for the model order. Each case is one tool's candidates (what the key can use at the level, in the tool's own order), the org's choice (null is automatic), and what must follow: the order the tool lists, the model it starts on by the choice alone (null: the tool's own rule), and, when given, Claude Code's slots. A choice places a tool's models when some candidate's base is in its list; a choice that places none of them is no choice for that tool. When it places some, the order is the placed candidates in list order, then the rest in the tool's own order, and the start model is the default when the tool has it, else the first of the order. Claude Code's model is the start model, else (no choice) the first opus, else the first sonnet, else the first. Its opus and sonnet aliases are the first of each tier in the order, falling back to its model. Its background model ignores the order: the preference list, else the first model in the tool's own order that is not claude-sonnet-5, else the first. context_window is 1000000 when the model is a 5-series model (the gateway reports no window for these candidates), else null. The launcher repo owns this file and the portal vendors it. Change the rule here first, then in both.",
